:"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"dan-h1835g","name":"Dan","kind":"place","brief":"In Dan","count":1,"firstVerse":25}],"words":[{"base":"H6635","lemma":"צָבָא","tr":"tsa·va","gloss":"army","lang":"h","inPassage":17,"uses":484},{"base":"H5265","lemma":"נָסַע","tr":"na·sa","gloss":"to set out","lang":"h","inPassage":9,"uses":146},{"base":"H4294","lemma":"מַטֶּה","tr":"mat·teh","gloss":"tribe: rod","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":252},{"base":"H1714","lemma":"דֶּ֫גֶל","tr":"de·gel","gloss":"standard","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":14},{"base":"H4264","lemma":"מַחֲנֶה","tr":"ma·cha·neh","gloss":"camp","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":215},{"base":"H4908","lemma":"מִשְׁכָּן","tr":"mish·kan","gloss":"tabernacle","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":139},{"base":"H6301","lemma":"פְּדָהצוּר","tr":"pe·da·h·tsur","gloss":"Pedahzur","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"H6701","lemma":"צוּרִישַׁדָּ֑י","tr":"tsu·ri·shad·day","gloss":"Zurishaddai","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"H4550","lemma":"מַסַּע","tr":"mas·sa","gloss":"journey","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"H6051","lemma":"עָנָן","tr":"a·nan","gloss":"cloud","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":87}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NUM","chapter":2,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"On the east side, toward the sunrise, the divisions of Judah are to camp under their standard: The leader of the descendants of Judah is Nahshon son of Amminadab,","from":14},{"book":"NUM","chapter":2,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"The total number of men in the divisions of the camp of Judah is 186,400; they shall set out first.","from":14},{"book":"NUM","chapter":2,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"On the south side, the divisions of Reuben are to camp under their standard: The leader of the Reubenites is Elizur son of Shedeur,","from":18},{"book":"NUM","chapter":2,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"The total number of men in the divisions of the camp of Reuben is 151,450; they shall set out second.","from":18},{"book":"JOS","chapter":6,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"While the horns continued to sound, the armed troops marched ahead of the priests who blew the horns, and the rear guard followed the ark.","from":25},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And while he was dwelling in the Wilderness of Paran, his mother got a wife for him from the land of Egypt.","from":12},{"book":"GEN","chapter":48,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But his father refused. “I know, my son, I know!” he said. “He too shall become a people, and he too shall be great; nevertheless, his younger brother shall be greater than he, and his offspring shall become a multitude of nations.”","from":22},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Judah, your brothers shall praise you. Your hand shall be on the necks of your enemies; your fatherʼs sons shall bow down to you.","from":14}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":10},{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":2},{"id":"judges-era","title":"Judges era and the road to David","people":2}]},"29-32":{"people":[{"id":"hobab-h2246","name":"Hobab","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Jethro","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"jethro-h3503","name":"Jethro","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Zipporah","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":1,"firstVerse":29}],"places":[{"id":"midian-h4080h","name":"Midian","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":29}],"words":[{"base":"H3190","lemma":"יָטַב","tr":"ya·tav","gloss":"be good","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":117},{"base":"H9032","lemma":"ךְ","tr":"kh","gloss":"you","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":333},{"base":"H2246","lemma":"חֹבָב","tr":"cho·vav","gloss":"Hobab","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H2896","lemma":"טוֹב","tr":"tov","gloss":"pleasant","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":538},{"base":"H4084","lemma":"מִדְיָנִי","tr":"mid·ya·ni","gloss":"Midianite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H4872","lemma":"מֹשֶׁה","tr":"mo·sheh","gloss":"Moses","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":766},{"base":"H7467","lemma":"רְעוּאֵל","tr":"re·u·el","gloss":"Reuel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"H5973","lemma":"עִם","tr":"im","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1051},{"base":"H4138","lemma":"מוֹלֶ֫דֶת","tr":"mo·le·det","gloss":"relatives","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":22},{"base":"H2859","lemma":"חֹתֵן","tr":"cho·ten","gloss":"relative","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":33}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Then the Lordappeared to Abram and said, “I will give this land to your offspring.” So Abram built an altar there to the Lord, who had appeared to him.","from":29},{"book":"JOB","chapter":29,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"I served as eyes to the blind and as feet to the lame.","from":31},{"book":"EXO","chapter":2,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"When the daughters returned to their father Reuel, he asked them, “Why have you returned so early today?”","from":29},{"book":"EXO","chapter":3,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Meanwhile, Moses was shepherding the flock of his father-in-law Jethro, the priest of Midian. He led the flock to the far side of the wilderness and came to Horeb, the mountain of God.","from":29},{"book":"JDG","chapter":4,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now Heber the Kenite had moved away from the Kenites, the descendants of Hobab the father-in-law of Moses, and had pitched his tent by the great tree of Zaanannim, which was near Kedesh.","from":29},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the Lordsaid to Abram, “Leave your country, your kindred, and your fatherʼs household, and go to the land I will show you.","from":30},{"book":"GEN","chapter":13,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"for all the land that you see, I will give to you and your offspring forever.","from":29},{"book":"GEN","chapter":15,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"On that day the Lordmade a covenant with Abram, saying, “To your descendants I have given this land—from the river of Egypt to the great River Euphrates—","from":29}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":2}]},"33-36":{"people":[{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":1,"firstVerse":35},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":36}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H5265","lemma":"נָסַע","tr":"na·sa","gloss":"to set out","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":146},{"base":"H0727","lemma":"אֲרוֹן","tr":"a·ron","gloss":"ark","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":202},{"base":"H7969","lemma":"שָׁלֹשׁ","tr":"sha·losh","gloss":"three","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":431},{"base":"H1870","lemma":"דֶּ֫רֶךְ","tr":"de·rekh","gloss":"way: conduct","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":706},{"base":"H7233","lemma":"רְבָבָה","tr":"re·va·vah","gloss":"myriad","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"H4496","lemma":"מְנוּחָה","tr":"me·nu·chah","gloss":"Nohah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":22},{"base":"H8446","lemma":"תּוּר","tr":"tur","gloss":"to spy","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H3119","lemma":"יוֹמָם","tr":"yo·mam","gloss":"by day","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":50},{"base":"H6327","lemma":"פּוּץ","tr":"puts","gloss":"to scatter","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":67},{"base":"H6051","lemma":"עָנָן","tr":"a·nan","gloss":"cloud","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":87}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":68,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"God arises. His enemies are scattered, and those who hate Him flee His presence.","from":35},{"book":"PSA","chapter":68,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"As smoke is blown away, You will drive them out; as wax melts before the fire, the wicked will perish in the presence of God.","from":35},{"book":"GEN","chapter":24,"verse":60,"verseEnd":60,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And they blessed Rebekah and said to her, “Our sister, may you become the mother of thousands upon thousands. May your offspring possess the gates of their enemies.”","from":36},{"book":"EXO","chapter":3,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Meanwhile, Moses was shepherding the flock of his father-in-law Jethro, the priest of Midian. He led the flock to the far side of the wilderness and came to Horeb, the mountain of God.","from":33},{"book":"EXO","chapter":13,"verse":21,"verseEnd":22,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the LORD went before them in a pillar of cloud to guide their way by day, and in a pillar of fire to give them light by night, so that they could travel by day or night. Neither the pillar of cloud by day nor the pillar of fire by night left its place before the people.","from":34},{"book":"EXO","chapter":19,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Moses went up to God, and the LORD called to him from the mountain, “This is what you are to tell the house of Jacob and explain to the sons of Israel:","from":33},{"book":"EXO","chapter":24,"verse":17,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the sight of the glory of the LORD was like a consuming fire on the mountaintop in the eyes of the Israelites. Moses entered the cloud as he went up on the mountain, and he remained on the mountain forty days and forty nights.","from":33},{"book":"EXO","chapter":33,"verse":14,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the LORD answered, “My Presence will go with you, and I will give you rest.” “If Your Presence does not go with us,” Moses replied, “do not lead us up from here.","from":33}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}